    <section class="lf-guide-faq">
      <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
      <details><summary>When is the best month to advertise Christmas light installation?</summary><p>It depends on the market and available installation slots. Prepare before peak season and test earlier campaigns where customer demand supports them.</p></details>
<details><summary>Should installers advertise all year?</summary><p>Not necessarily with paid ads. Year-round work can include SEO, customer retention, creative preparation, tracking and commercial outreach, while campaign spending follows demand.</p></details>
<details><summary>Should commercial Christmas lighting marketing start earlier?</summary><p>Often it should be considered earlier because approval and quotation processes can take longer, but timing varies by buyer.</p></details>
<details><summary>How do I avoid wasting advertising budget late in the season?</summary><p>Connect marketing to real crew capacity, update availability messages, monitor search intent and pause or adjust acquisition when suitable installation slots are unavailable.</p></details>
<details><summary>What is the first automation a Christmas light installer needs?</summary><p>Reliable lead capture, owner assignment and appropriate acknowledgment are a practical starting point before adding more elaborate follow-up.</p></details>
    </section>

